    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "04ff3f22",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "04ff3f22"
      },
      "source": [
        "So, to recap:\n",
        "\n",
        "- a **row**: `income.loc[90]`, or a range `income.loc[90:95]`\n",
        "- a **column**: `income[\"column name\"]`\n",
        "- a **cell**: `income.loc[90, \"column name\"]`\n",
        "\n",
        "`.iloc[]` does the same by *position* (0, 1, 2, ...) rather than by label; see the [pandas documentation](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/user_guide/indexing.html).\n",
        "\n",
        "### Exercise\n",
        "\n",
        "How do the equivalised incomes of single adults (`\"Single adult\"`) and childless couples (`\"Childless couple, annual income\"`) compare? Look at the 1st, 50th and 99th percentiles and summarise what this tells you about the value, or price, of coupling."
      ]
    },
