    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "84bd0520",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "84bd0520"
      },
      "source": [
        "The curve is roughly linear in the middle, but rises steeply at the top.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Exercise: means\n",
        "\n",
        "Where does the mean appear here? Draw a horizontal line for the **mean** with `plt.axhline`, and one for the **median** on the same graph. Which is higher, and why? What does the median mean in this context?\n",
        "\n",
        "Hint: last week we used `axvline` to draw vertical lines; `axhline` draws horizontal ones."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 16,
      "id": "e5a96de1",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.756526Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.756446Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.762542Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.759702Z"
        },
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 472
        },
        "id": "e5a96de1",
        "outputId": "3a51ef52-bde4-4757-d054-f31c029f6291"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot the main data curve\n",
        "income[weekly].plot()\n",
        "plt.title(\"UK net equivalised household income by percentile, 2010-11\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Income percentile\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Income per week (GBP)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate mean and median for the plotted weekly column\n",
        "mean_val = income[weekly].mean()\n",
        "median_val = income[weekly].median()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Draw the horizontal lines before showing the plot\n",
        "plt.axhline(mean_val, color='r', linestyle='--', label=f'Mean: £{mean_val:.2f}')\n",
        "plt.axhline(median_val, color='g', linestyle='-.', label=f'Median: £{median_val:.2f}')\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
