      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "62f07864",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "62f07864"
      },
      "source": [
        "Only the weekly column is a number (`float64`). Let's look at one of the other values:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "da22b5e7",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.907295Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.907233Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.908855Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.908502Z"
        },
        "id": "da22b5e7",
        "outputId": "459de4a6-bd85-44f2-d12a-228c6d6b169e"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "'14,627.95'"
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 13,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "income.loc[50, \"Single adult\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "d310060f",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d310060f"
      },
      "source": [
        "`'14,627.95'` is a piece of **text** (a string), not a number. The commas make it easier for people to read, but they confuse software. Missing values are sometimes written as `-`, which causes the same problem. In general, some detective work is needed to figure out what's wrong with a data file: looking at the raw values, or opening the file in a text editor, is often the quickest way.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Example: cleaning data\n",
        "\n",
        "We'll make a new dataframe with just the two columns we're interested in, remove the commas with `.replace()`, and convert the result to numbers with `.astype(float)`:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "4bc71733",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.909715Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.909664Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.912648Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.912409Z"
        },
        "id": "4bc71733",
        "outputId": "d21acfcf-7067-471b-dbb6-4a170fbfe09a"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/html": [
              "<div>\n",
