            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 14,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "clean = income[[\"Childless couple, annual income\", \"Couple, two children under 14\"]]\n",
        "clean = clean.replace(\",\", \"\", regex=True).astype(float)\n",
        "clean.head()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "d9bdf2bd",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d9bdf2bd"
      },
      "source": [
        "(**Extension:** `regex` stands for *regular expression*, a powerful way of searching and replacing text. It's beyond the scope of this class, but worth looking into.)\n",
        "\n",
        "Now the plot works:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "53badca0",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.913594Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.913541Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.955089Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.954761Z"
        },
        "id": "53badca0",
        "outputId": "2fa85704-db7e-47ea-f819-16d400dee045"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "image/png": "",
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1000x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "clean.plot()\n",
        "plt.title(\"A Modest Proposal: the fiscal benefits of childbirth\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Percentile\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Income per year (GBP)\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "88f1b27d",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "88f1b27d"
      },
      "source": [
        "This raises further questions. If the top 20% shows such a sharp increase, is there a similar uptick *within* the 1%? How does the curve break down by gender, education or ethnicity?\n",
        "\n",
        "### Exercise\n",
        "\n",
        "Repeat the cleaning and plotting for single adults and childless couples. Comment on the differences."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 20,
      "id": "78578c4a",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.956237Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.956180Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.957715Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.957318Z"
        },
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 472
        },
        "id": "78578c4a",
        "outputId": "6cb9e279-6871-4b78-814b-8d26fa7314cb"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "clean = income[[\"Single adult\", \"Childless couple, annual income\"]]\n",
        "clean = clean.replace(\",\", \"\", regex=True).astype(float)\n",
        "clean.head()\n",
        "\n",
        "clean.plot()\n",
        "plt.title(\"UK net equivalised household income by percentile, 2010-11\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Income Percentile\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Income per week (GBP)\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "093ff551",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "093ff551"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Filtering by value\n",
        "\n",
        "So far we've selected data by its label. What if we want to filter by **value**? For example, all childless couples with a net equivalised income above £50,000 a year:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "c64d5a32",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.958648Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.958596Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.961152Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.960847Z"
        },
        "id": "c64d5a32",
        "outputId": "255a1f9d-8d1d-4c80-d96a-ac0ec7bbd3c8"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/html": [
