      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "5a2d5bdd",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5a2d5bdd"
      },
      "source": [
        "Putting it inside `clean[ ]` keeps only the rows where it is `True`. Other comparison operators:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `==` is equal to (why the double equals?)\n",
        "- `!=` is not equal to\n",
        "- `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`\n",
        "\n",
        "### Exercise\n",
        "\n",
        "On an appropriately labelled graph, plot the incomes of all single adults whose net equivalised income is less than or equal to £10,000 a year. What proportion of the population is this?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 31,
      "id": "c922711d",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.965196Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.965145Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.966498Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-16T10:39:33.966174Z"
        },
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 472
        },
        "id": "c922711d",
        "outputId": "cfdb48e7-ffe5-4da1-d58b-cf1c206be8e5"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "low_income_single = clean[clean[\"Single adult\"] <= 10000]\n",
        "\n",
        "low_income_single[\"Single adult\"].plot()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.title(\"Incomes of Single Adults <= £10,000/year\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Income Percentile\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Income per year (GBP)\")\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "42730913",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "42730913"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Wide and long data\n",
        "\n",
        "Data that records the same units (countries, ships, firms) repeatedly over time comes in two layouts:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **wide**: one row per unit, one column per time period. Compact, and how most published tables look.\n",
        "- **long**: one row per unit × time period. More repetition, but it's what grouping, plotting and statistics expect.\n",
        "\n",
        "[Global Fishing Watch](https://globalfishingwatch.org) uses the signals that ships broadcast to estimate where and when vessels are fishing. This file gives **apparent fishing hours** per month for the ten flag states (countries a vessel is registered to) with the most fishing, 2017-2024, in **wide** format:\n",
        "\n",
        "*Data: Global Fishing Watch, [fishing effort v3](https://globalfishingwatch.org/dataset-and-code-fishing-effort/), CC BY-NC 4.0.*"
      ]
    },
